docs/cli-reference.md:3:Complete command-line reference for `openfang`, the CLI tool for the OpenFang Agent OS.
docs/cli-reference.md:7:The `openfang` binary is the primary interface for managing the OpenFang Agent OS. It supports two modes of operation:
docs/cli-reference.md:9:- **Daemon mode** -- When a daemon is running (`openfang start`), CLI commands communicate with it over HTTP. This is the recommended mode for production use.
docs/cli-reference.md:12:Running `openfang` with no subcommand launches the interactive TUI (terminal user interface) built with ratatui, which provides a full dashboard experience in the terminal.
docs/cli-reference.md:14:## Installation
docs/cli-reference.md:19:cargo install --path crates/openfang-cli
docs/cli-reference.md:25:cargo build --release -p openfang-cli
docs/cli-reference.md:26:# Binary: target/release/openfang (or openfang.exe on Windows)
docs/cli-reference.md:32:docker run -it openfang/openfang:latest
docs/cli-reference.md:35:### Shell installer
docs/cli-reference.md:38:curl -fsSL https://get.openfang.ai | sh
docs/cli-reference.md:47:| `--config <PATH>` | Path to a custom config file. Overrides the default `~/.openfang/config.toml`. |
docs/cli-reference.md:49:| `--version` | Print the version of the `openfang` binary. |
docs/cli-reference.md:55:| `RUST_LOG` | Controls log verbosity (e.g. `info`, `debug`, `openfang_kernel=trace`). |
docs/cli-reference.md:57:| `EDITOR` / `VISUAL` | Editor used by `openfang config edit`. Falls back to `notepad` (Windows) or `vi` (Unix). |
docs/cli-reference.md:63:### openfang (no subcommand)
docs/cli-reference.md:68:openfang [--config <PATH>]
docs/cli-reference.md:71:The TUI provides a full-screen terminal interface with panels for agents, chat, workflows, channels, skills, settings, and more. Tracing output is redirected to `~/.openfang/tui.log` to avoid corrupting the terminal display.
